<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica money mkt shortage falls to 9.378 bln rand.</title>
<headline>SAfrica money mkt shortage falls to 9.378 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage fell to 9.378 billion rand on Wednesday from 9.697 billion rand on Tuesday, the Reserve Bank said.  </p>
<p>Banks quoted their three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 16.95 percent and 17.00 percent offered and 17.10 and 17.20 percent bid, while the 90-day BA rate was also unmoved at between 16.30 and 16.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
